                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "210310d2-26db-4e71-9163-0c84fb6d530f",
                        "source_entry_id": "42962df7-7b26-3862-9658-b1e5f33240e0",
                        "source_sense_id": "a0430286-4d8b-39eb-9f6c-55eeea45998f",
                        "target_lang_word": "verbosity",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "verbosity",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d060a185-e26e-3e44-a82d-14db9a626de3",
                                        "entry_id": "b43864c4-e3e5-38fd-9357-3f68eb47733b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The excess use of words, especially using more than are needed for clarity or precision."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "rhetoric",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e8de8d2f-2570-4ac4-82a5-a981939da822",
                                                "sense_id": "d060a185-e26e-3e44-a82d-14db9a626de3",
                                                "text": "With Christie's words about \"all-talk-no-action\" in mind, notice that Obama and his two secretaries of state, Hillary Clinton and John Kerry, as well as his vice president, Joe Biden, were all senators, the last two serving for two or three decades, respectively. Not forgetting the ill-fated secretary of defense, Senator Chuck Hagel. Their capacity for talking so much and saying so little is astonishing. Their verbosity is unpalatable."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "444f76fd-50db-48bd-bd07-a2fcc61a1485",
                        "source_entry_id": "42962df7-7b26-3862-9658-b1e5f33240e0",
                        "source_sense_id": "a0430286-4d8b-39eb-9f6c-55eeea45998f",
                        "target_lang_word": "loquacity",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "loquacity",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "305a921b-8b2d-3dc7-8ce7-6189e9646e66",
                                        "entry_id": "6c7f2ce3-c14d-3ab7-9633-b7f43e954f97",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Talkativeness; the quality of being loquacious."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "01e315bd-fb76-4200-92fe-8d95c9b84b79",
                                                "sense_id": "305a921b-8b2d-3dc7-8ce7-6189e9646e66",
                                                "text": "A man that were ſo diſpoſed, may ſeeme in reaſon to reproove […] the loquacity of Euripides, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "baf63779-a856-4667-a857-d2bfbab337dc",
                                                "sense_id": "305a921b-8b2d-3dc7-8ce7-6189e9646e66",
                                                "text": "Neither is eloquence or rhetoric unclaimed by him: he perſuaded with Stentorian loquacity, and convinces by the irreſiſtible powers of a bellowing horſe laugh."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ce46f9b2-c1ae-421e-987e-16c09225cd33",
                                                "sense_id": "305a921b-8b2d-3dc7-8ce7-6189e9646e66",
                                                "text": "Their silence would have been awkward but for the loquacity of Jane, who talked enough for all three."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b25c26b9-5722-4820-950c-923fe5a22b94",
                                                "sense_id": "305a921b-8b2d-3dc7-8ce7-6189e9646e66",
                                                "text": "Here was news for us, for Mr Kelada, with all his loquacity, had never told anyone what his business was."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "18500ab3-d2fd-4205-91eb-2b9ccbc92905",
                        "source_entry_id": "42962df7-7b26-3862-9658-b1e5f33240e0",
                        "source_sense_id": "a0430286-4d8b-39eb-9f6c-55eeea45998f",
                        "target_lang_word": "verbiage",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "verbiage",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "844fc8e3-f123-3cc7-9121-945ee313b0ff",
                                        "entry_id": "d742aadf-b763-3811-8a65-e15e2039aba1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Overabundance of words."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "32031b74-035d-4f7c-b468-5a69a0ec2518",
                                                "sense_id": "844fc8e3-f123-3cc7-9121-945ee313b0ff",
                                                "text": "bureaucratic verbiage"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c63b9132-39bc-4263-aaab-511ede4a5fb5",
                                                "sense_id": "844fc8e3-f123-3cc7-9121-945ee313b0ff",
                                                "text": "We're done drafting our paper except for the final check to see whether any verbiage can be reduced."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3d0e9524-9dee-43a5-b2d9-84b5a91bbb41",
                                                "sense_id": "844fc8e3-f123-3cc7-9121-945ee313b0ff",
                                                "text": "A very garrulous person, he approached the counter in a fog of verbiage."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6b399bb7-db7e-370b-9b12-a887abb3afd1",
                                        "entry_id": "d742aadf-b763-3811-8a65-e15e2039aba1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The manner in which something is expressed in words; word choice."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3636fcb6-238c-4473-963f-dd947ed084d1",
                                                "sense_id": "6b399bb7-db7e-370b-9b12-a887abb3afd1",
                                                "text": "Near-synonyms: phrasing; terminology; phraseology"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "94f94620-fc69-43f0-a057-0cff43257d44",
                                                "sense_id": "6b399bb7-db7e-370b-9b12-a887abb3afd1",
                                                "text": "In each article of this series, there is a paragraph on nutrition; the verbiage for it was developed by consensus among the section editors, and therefore no elective rewording should be done (by others) in any such paragraph."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "206da4fa-8c60-417d-b6f7-17a24ba72580",
                                                "sense_id": "6b399bb7-db7e-370b-9b12-a887abb3afd1",
                                                "text": "We're done drafting our paper except for the final verbiage on fire safety, which will be supplied by the safety engineers."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "00b5be41-04ba-4f08-aca6-a8d29777ec1f",
                                                "sense_id": "6b399bb7-db7e-370b-9b12-a887abb3afd1",
                                                "text": "The comparison of coincidences in the verbiage of different languages, and affinity of etymological formation, are interesting subjects of philological investigation."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "08fd4444-e720-49ae-8cad-e1e248cf7e32",
                                                "sense_id": "6b399bb7-db7e-370b-9b12-a887abb3afd1",
                                                "text": "Use concise military verbiage."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "67da84d9-e9de-4a0f-b507-16162d3d04de",
                        "source_entry_id": "42962df7-7b26-3862-9658-b1e5f33240e0",
                        "source_sense_id": "a0430286-4d8b-39eb-9f6c-55eeea45998f",
                        "target_lang_word": "loquacité",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "loquacité",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6d8ef0c2-d2d7-3050-8d05-ebe343e21d43",
                                        "entry_id": "dc5dfe6f-cb88-373a-8619-24c174b28152",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Habitude de parler beaucoup ; tendance au bavardage ; état de celui ou de celle qui est loquace."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2429dfc5-4827-4a3b-aa56-3485634feb5d",
                                                "sense_id": "6d8ef0c2-d2d7-3050-8d05-ebe343e21d43",
                                                "text": "Cette rencontre était de nature à vivement frapper madame de Staël ; à son retour au château, elle en parla peu, malgré le besoin d’expansion qui, chez elle, dégénérait en loquacité ; mais elle en parut fortement préoccupée."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "afe61f3f-4a09-4f2e-b5be-fae86ba39fdd",
                                                "sense_id": "6d8ef0c2-d2d7-3050-8d05-ebe343e21d43",
                                                "text": "Quoique très instruite, elle n’avoit ni les caprices, ni l’humeur qu’on attribue aux gens de lettres, qui tantôt se livrent à une loquacité importune, tantôt se renferment dans un silence méprisant."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ebf92101-99de-460f-b98c-5d90a7b4eaf5",
                                                "sense_id": "6d8ef0c2-d2d7-3050-8d05-ebe343e21d43",
                                                "text": "Comme si l’ivresse eût délié sa langue, l’ivresse qui met dans la bouche des hommes un balbutiement pareil à la voix des bêtes, lui, dès qu’il était saoul, devenait d’une loquacité terrible."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "274f5946-14dc-44a9-bb66-5e91d7559bbe",
                                                "sense_id": "6d8ef0c2-d2d7-3050-8d05-ebe343e21d43",
                                                "text": "Pendant un moment, la morgue germanique lutta en lui avec la simplicité anglaise, et aussi avec sa bienveillance naturelle et sa loquacité, et elle eut le dessous."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7599b54f-a532-4994-9c89-86844addd296",
                                                "sense_id": "6d8ef0c2-d2d7-3050-8d05-ebe343e21d43",
                                                "text": "L’un était […] probablement silencieux par ordre ; l’autre, gêné de trouver Mikkelsen et Münck parlant sa langue, était d’une loquacité un peu déconcertante."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0a430d1e-8822-33b1-8fae-98753529f7ad",
                                        "entry_id": "dc5dfe6f-cb88-373a-8619-24c174b28152",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Logorrhée."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dated"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6c3472f6-8168-4bb0-bb75-6975b1a73ede",
                                                "sense_id": "0a430d1e-8822-33b1-8fae-98753529f7ad",
                                                "text": "Ces sortes de réveils étaient marquées par un cri aigu et par la projection des membres, tantôt d’un côté, tantôt d’un autre, et les premiers jours par une loquacité semi-délirante qui n’inquiétait pas moins que la stupeur."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
